<SiteLayout title="Privacy and Personal Data" description="Information about MNEMORİSK contact form and the currently disabled visitor analytics.">
<div class="wrap">
  <section class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / DATA PROTECTION</div><h1>Privacy and personal data protection</h1><p>Current contact services and future, currently disabled website analytics are described separately.</p></section>
  <article class="privacy-content">
    <section>
      <h2>1. Project and identity of the data controller</h2>
      <p>MNEMORİSK is a research project conducted at Erzincan Binali Yıldırım University and awarded support under the TÜBİTAK 1001 Programme (project no. 226K193). Associate Professor Akın Bakioğlu, the principal investigator, coordinates the website's technical and editorial operation. Contact: <a href="mailto:mnemorisk@gmail.com">mnemorisk@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Data controller:</strong> Associate Professor Akın Bakioğlu. I determine the purposes and means of processing for the website's contact form and the proposed website analytics. Requests concerning personal data can be directed to <a href="mailto:mnemorisk@gmail.com">mnemorisk@gmail.com</a>. This notice does not replace any separate institutional or ethics arrangements applicable to the project's surveys and interviews.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>2. Current contact form: information and purposes</h2>
      <p>If you choose to send a message, the form collects your <strong>name, email address, selected subject and message</strong> to receive, consider and respond to your enquiry. FormSubmit and network providers may separately process technical connection information, including IP addresses and browser/request logs, in delivering and securing the form. These are not saved to the MNEMORİSK visitor-analytics database.</p>
      <p>Form information is collected directly from you when you submit the electronic form. For receiving, handling and responding to enquiries, the processing basis is <strong>legitimate interests under Article 5(2)(f) of Turkish Law No. 6698</strong>, provided that processing does not prejudice the individual's fundamental rights and freedoms. Form submission is not presented as separate explicit consent.</p>
      <p>Alternatively, email <a href="mailto:mnemorisk@gmail.com">mnemorisk@gmail.com</a>. Do not include identity documents, national ID numbers, health information, confidential material about research participants or sensitive third-party information.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>3. Service providers and transfers abroad</h2>
      <p>The website is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. <strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides domain and analytics infrastructure. Contact form submissions go directly to <a href="https://formsubmit.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FormSubmit</a> and are then forwarded to the project mailbox. Form fields and associated technical connection information may be processed by those providers; the email provider may also handle received messages.</p>
      <p><strong>MNEMORİSK does not separately send contact messages abroad as a research dataset.</strong> However, submitting the contact form necessarily transmits the supplied information to the FormSubmit service. The countries in which FormSubmit, GitHub Pages, Cloudflare and the email provider process operational or security-related personal information have not been independently verified for each service. It would therefore be misleading to claim that no personal data can be transferred abroad. If processing involves an international transfer, the conditions of <strong>Article 9 of Law No. 6698</strong> apply. See the <a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/8143/Kisisel-Verilerin-Yurt-Disina-Aktarilmasi-Rehberi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Authority's guide on international transfers (in Turkish)</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>4. Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p><a href="https://formsubmit.co/help" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FormSubmit states in its published documentation</a> that it retains submissions for 30 days. This is the provider's statement and does not imply that logs or copies held elsewhere have the same retention period.</p>
      <p>Messages are retained in the project mailbox to reply to enquiries and handle necessary follow-up; unnecessary correspondence is deleted when no longer needed. Under normal circumstances, the target retention period is <strong>no more than one year after the correspondence ends</strong>. Because the mailbox, deleted-items folder and service backups may have different retention processes, immediate removal of every copy is not claimed. Records may be retained longer where required by law or in connection with disputes. Contact messages are not maintained as a permanent research-participant dataset.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>5. Cookies and planned website analytics</h2>
      <p><strong>MNEMORİSK's own visitor analytics is currently disabled.</strong> The website does not currently use its own advertising or analytics cookies or a persistent identifier linking visits across days. Third-party verification screens used by the contact service, and the security and operational systems of service providers, may use their own cookies or network logs; this notice does not claim that all providers process no data.</p>
      <p>The proposed analytics system would record: page path and timestamp, country and broad region code, referring domain, device category, browser and content language, restricted campaign tags, internal navigation, scroll depth, estimated active viewing duration, download activity and external-link click categories/targets. It is not designed to store complete URL query strings, fragments, free-form text, form content, raw IP addresses or precise locations in the analytics database.</p>
      <p>The design computes a <strong>daily HMAC-based identifier</strong> from the connection's IP address and browser information without writing the raw IP to the analytics database. The identifier is programmed to be cleared within <strong>14 days</strong> after daily processing; detailed event data has a <strong>180-day</strong> retention ceiling, followed by summary data. The HMAC identifier must not be represented as anonymous personal data, and absence of a persistent cross-visit identifier does not eliminate data-protection obligations.</p>
      <p>The proposed client does not write analytics identifiers to cookies, localStorage or sessionStorage. The separate consent preference (accepted or rejected) is stored in the browser's localStorage so the visitor need not answer the same question repeatedly; it is not used to track browsing. A temporary random page-view identifier exists in browser memory, while sessions are calculated on the server. The design respects <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong>. Data would not be used for advertising targeting or made available on a public dashboard. Automated email reports and transfer of aggregated monthly snapshots to a separate private GitHub repository are also currently disabled.</p>
      <p><strong>This section documents an intended technical design, not analytics already being carried out or a confirmed legal basis.</strong> When activated, analytics will not start until the visitor actively chooses “Accept analytics”. The equally visible “Reject analytics” choice leaves the site fully usable; the choice can later be changed through “Analytics preferences” in the footer. Silence, browsing or dismissing a panel is not considered consent. Before activation, the Article 5 processing basis and any applicable Article 9 international-transfer obligations must be assessed, and this notice updated to reflect actual processing. Being cookie-free alone does not settle the question of consent. See the <a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/7275/2022-229" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Authority's decision 2022/229 concerning analytics cookies (in Turkish)</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>6. Your rights and submitting a request</h2>
      <p>Under Article 11 of Law No. 6698, you have rights including learning whether your personal data is processed, requesting information on processing, learning the purposes and recipients of data, and requesting rectification or erasure where legal conditions are met.</p>
      <p>Under Article 13, validly submitted requests must be answered <strong>within 30 days at the latest</strong>. Formal requests can be submitted in writing or through recognized methods such as registered electronic mail (KEP), qualified electronic signature, mobile signature or an email address previously provided to and registered with the controller. The relevant identification, contact and request details must be supplied through the legally appropriate channel. <strong>Do not send identity documents or national ID numbers through the ordinary contact form.</strong> Contact <a href="mailto:mnemorisk@gmail.com">mnemorisk@gmail.com</a> to identify an appropriate application channel.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/2046/Ilgili-Kisiler-Tarafindan-Yapilan-Basvurularin-Cevaplanmasi-Yukumlulugu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Authority guidance on responding to requests (in Turkish)</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>7. Scope and updates</h2>
      <p>This notice concerns only the website, contact form and proposed website analytics. It does not replace the information notices, research ethics procedures or consent processes for the project's surveys, interviews or fieldwork.</p>
      <p>Changes and the latest revision date will appear on this page. Official sources: <a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/2033/Aydinlatma-Yukumlulugu-" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information obligation</a>, <a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/4132/aydinlatma-yukumlulugunun-yerine-getirilmesinde-uyulacak-usul-ve-esaslar-hakkinda-teblig" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Notice Communiqué</a>, and <a href="https://www.kvkk.gov.tr/Icerik/2053/Yurtdisina-Aktarim" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">International transfers</a> (in Turkish).</p>
    </section>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 25 November 2026 · Existing services and proposed analytics are described separately.</p>
  </article>
</div>
